Now it is night.
It is my first night in Copenhagen.
I am in the bathroom.
It is very small.
There is a sink.
My toothbrush is red.
I put toothpaste on my toothbrush.
I brush my teeth.
The water is cold.
I wash my face.
It is nice.
I go over to my bed.
The bed is narrow.
But it is warm and soft.
I am lying under the duvet now.
My phone is lying on the table.
I set my alarm.
It rings at eight o'clock tomorrow.
I am tired, but I am ready.
Goodnight, Copenhagen.
